Package: fdmethods
Type: Package
Title: Frequency Domain Methods: Goertzel Algorithm and Sliding DFT
Version: 1.0
Date: 2024-01-01
Author: Helena Schmidt
Maintainer: Helena Schmidt <helena.schmidt@ktrask.de>
Description: Provides two frequency-domain analysis methods: the Goertzel
  algorithm for evaluating individual DFT terms without computing a full FFT
  (useful for targeted tone detection such as DTMF decoding), and the Sliding
  Discrete Fourier Transform (SlidingDFT) for maintaining a running DFT over a
  fixed-size window of real-valued samples. Both methods are available as C and
  C++ libraries; the Goertzel algorithm also has R and Python interfaces.
License: GPL (>= 2)
SystemRequirements: C++20
NeedsCompilation: yes
Imports: Rcpp (>= 0.12.3)
LinkingTo: Rcpp
